[
    {
        "content": "<p>I need the Manifold structure on <code>Circle × Circle</code> in a Physlib definition, but I wasn't able to find this instance. Is there even a <code>IsManifold</code> instance for <code>Circle</code>?<br>\nIf not, would this be welcome in mathlib? (And is <code>Circle</code> the correct thing to look at or should I use <code>Real.Angle</code> or <code>AddCircle</code> or something else?)</p>",
        "id": 593580770,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1778174103
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Geometry/Manifold/Instances/Sphere.html#instIsManifoldRealEuclideanSpaceFinOfNatNatModelWithCornersSelfTopWithTopENatCircle\">https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Geometry/Manifold/Instances/Sphere.html#instIsManifoldRealEuclideanSpaceFinOfNatNatModelWithCornersSelfTopWithTopENatCircle</a></p>",
        "id": 593585551,
        "sender_full_name": "Yongxi Lin (Aaron)",
        "timestamp": 1778175377
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"652766\">Christian Krause</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Manifold.20instance.20for.20Complex.2ECircle/near/593580770\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I need the Manifold structure on <code>Circle × Circle</code> in a Physlib definition</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Do you want your model space for <code>Circle × Circle</code> to be <code>(EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)) × (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1))</code>? (actually I guess it will even be <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ModelProd#doc\">docs#ModelProd</a> ...)</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(And is <code>Circle</code> the correct thing to look at or should I use <code>Real.Angle</code> or <code>AddCircle</code> or something else?)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Probably depends on what you're doing?</p>",
        "id": 593591935,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1778177126
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think having EuclianSpace R Fin 2 as the model space would also be nice, but I am not really sure what the difference between EuclianSpace R Fin 2, Fin 2 -&gt; EuclianSpace or the Product Space is. Is there documentation on that?<br>\n(Thank you for pointing out ModelProd, this explains why the normal one didnt work)<br>\nRe: what am i doing?<br>\nI am trying to implement the configuration space of a coplanar double pendulum (which is spanned by two parameters phi1 and phi2 from 0 to 2 pi. <br>\n(Sorry for the terrible formatting, I'm on mobile)</p>",
        "id": 593617230,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1778184674
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"652766\">Christian Krause</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Manifold.20instance.20for.20Complex.2ECircle/near/593617230\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I am not really sure what the difference between EuclianSpace R Fin 2, Fin 2 -&gt; EuclianSpace or the Product Space is. Is there documentation on that?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>L2 norm vs L∞ norm I believe, see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Prod.metricSpaceMax#doc\">docs#Prod.metricSpaceMax</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=metricSpacePi#doc\">docs#metricSpacePi</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Prod.dist_eq#doc\">docs#Prod.dist_eq</a></p>",
        "id": 593621641,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1778185828
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>All norms on finite-dimensional EuclideanSpace are equivalent, so it should be fine to work with <code>ModelProd (EuclideanSpace R (Fin 1)) (EuclideanSpace R (Fin 1))</code>. If you <em>really</em> wanted to work over <code>EucideanSpace R (Fin 2)</code>, you could use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=EuclideanSpace.finAddEquivProd#doc\">docs#EuclideanSpace.finAddEquivProd</a> and then compose with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ModelWithCorners.transContinuousLinearEquiv#doc\">docs#ModelWithCorners.transContinuousLinearEquiv</a>. </p>\n<p>This is a place where a cleaner API could be useful (as well as a canonical implementation of \"the torus\" in <code>Geometry/Manifold/Instances</code>).</p>",
        "id": 593631003,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1778189175
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that there's notation <code>𝓡 1</code> (in the <code>Manifold</code> namespace) for the canonical model with corners on <code>EuclideanSpace ℝ Fin 1</code> (<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Geometry/Manifold/Instances/Real.html\">docs</a>)</p>",
        "id": 593634568,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1778190609
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree there should be an implementation of \"the torus\" --- the issue is that there are multiple possible presentations (e.g., S¹ × S¹ or <code>ℂ / ℤ</code> or more general lattices)... so a predicate \"I am a torus\" also is useful, and now you have a can of worms. I remember <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1013125\">@Yury Kudryashov (Harmonic)</span> asking about this a while back, but am not sure if a canonical answer ever emerged.</p>",
        "id": 593634757,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1778190705
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That zulip thread was <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"116395\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/116395-maths/topic/Torus.3A.20quotient.20or.20pi.3F/with/471052558\">#maths &gt; Torus: quotient or pi?</a></p>",
        "id": 593637100,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1778191645
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><del>Big missunderstanding on my part</del></p>",
        "id": 594320082,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1778511137
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>Full mwe</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Manifold</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsManifold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝓘</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">,(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: failed to synthesize instance of type class</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  ChartedSpace (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)) (Circle × Circle)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">Hint: Type class instance resolution failures can be inspected with the `set_option trace.Meta.synthInstance true` command.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsManifold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝓘</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">,(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ChartedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ModelProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: failed to synthesize instance of type class</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  NormedAddCommGroup (ModelProd (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)) (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">Hint: Type class instance resolution failures can be inspected with the `set_option trace.Meta.synthInstance true` command.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">---</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: failed to synthesize instance of type class</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  NormedAddCommGroup (ModelProd (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)) (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">Hint: Type class instance resolution failures can be inspected with the `set_option trace.Meta.synthInstance true` command.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsManifold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝓘</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">ModelProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ModelProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- ModelProd of normed groups, using the sup norm. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- Product of normed groups, using the sup norm. -/</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ModelProd</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">normedCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ModelProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ModelProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: failed to synthesize instance of type class</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  NormedSpace ℝ (ModelProd (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)) (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">Hint: Type class instance resolution failures can be inspected with the `set_option trace.Meta.synthInstance true` command.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">---</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: failed to synthesize instance of type class</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  NormedSpace ℝ (ModelProd (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)) (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)))</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">Hint: Type class instance resolution failures can be inspected with the `set_option trace.Meta.synthInstance true` command.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsManifold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝓘</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">ModelProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>",
